# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.


---

## 2026.04.19 - Part 2: Proof of Concept

### Added
- Created initial TaskManager proof-of-concept class
- Implemented basic task storage using ArrayList
- Added ability to:
  - add tasks
  - remove tasks by index
  - mark tasks as completed
  - display all tasks
  - get total task count
- Created inner Task class to store task data


---

## 2026.04.20 - Part 3: Interfaces

### Added
- Created `TaskManagerKernel` interface defining core functionality:
  - addTask
  - removeTask
  - completeTask
  - getTaskCount
  - getTaskName
  - isTaskCompleted
- Created `TaskManager` interface extending kernel
- Defined abstract methods:
  - toString()
  - equals(Object)

### Changed
- Separated implementation from specification using interface-based design


---

## 2026.04.22 - Part 4: Abstract Class

### Added
- Created `TaskManagerSecondary` abstract class
- Implemented reusable methods:
  - toString() (formatted task display)
  - equals() (deep comparison of TaskManager objects)

### Changed
- Moved shared logic from implementation into abstract class to reduce duplication

### Notes
- This class provides secondary operations built on top of kernel methods
- Prepares system for final kernel implementation in Part 5


## 2026.04.23 - Part 5: Kernel Implementation

### Added
- Implemented `TaskManager1L` kernel class
- Added full working data representation using ArrayList
- Implemented all kernel methods:
  - addTask
  - removeTask
  - completeTask
  - getTaskCount
  - getTaskName
  - isTaskCompleted

### Changed
- Connected implementation to abstract class for inherited functionality

### Notes
- This is the main functional component of the system


---

## 2026.04.24 - Part 6: Finishing Touches

### Added
- Created JUnit test suite for kernel and abstract class
- Added use-case demonstrations showing real-world usage
- Added CHANGELOG and polished documentation
- Organized project structure for submission

### Changed
- Improved code readability and consistency
- Finalized component for submission

### Notes
- Project now includes:
  - proof-of-concept
  - interfaces
  - abstract class
  - kernel implementation
  - tests
  - use cases
